        'c1ce104d-076e-4eaa-b464-06467a67ddcd'::uuid,
        'Fair Game',
        'Supplemental',
        '13',
        'Monstrosity (Shapechanger)',
        ARRAY['VRGR']::text[],
        '- As per server rules, a PC cursed with lycanthropy normally can''t be played in another game until the lycanthropy is removed and becomes an NPC under the DM''s control during the full moon. Given the nature of loup garou lycanthropy, the character can only be played in adventures taken for the purpose of finding and killing the loup garou that cursed them so as to make it possible to cure their lycanthropy.
- Lycanthropy from this creature can also be removed via a Wish spell or Divine Intervention (2014) even if the loup garou is still alive. A PC can benefit from Divine Intervention (2014) to cure loup garou lycanthropy in this way only once in their career.
- After the loup garou has been slain and if Remove Curse is used on the cursed PC, the affected PC must roll their DC 17 Constitution saving throw in #downtime-logs. On a successful save, the PC must then expend 3 DTP to clear exhaustion accrued from the ordeal. On a failed save, the PC must either wait 30 real life days or expend 30 DTP (or the remainder in DTP of days remaining) before another attempt at Remove Curse can be made.',
        19310.0::double precision
